0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A SPECIAL MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, JANUARY 2, 2008\r\rMayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:00 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 7:01 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\rPending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a): Calabasas Ridge HOA v. Gordon, LC 079145; Smith v. City of Calabasas, BS 106644; Cooper v. Calabasas Park Estates Owners Association,�BC 323695; Toby Keeler and Elizabeth Stephens v. City of Calabasas, BS 109503; Parks v. City of Calabasas, BC 382012.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:40 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:45 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Lysik, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Erik and Elsa Pontoppidan.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, reported that there was no reportable action in closed session.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor Bozajian presented a proclamation to Mike Gowen, Plant Manager for Lupin Hill Elementary School, in recognition of his heroic actions in coming to the aid of a local resident whose home caught on fire. Mayor Bozajian announced that the Chamber of Commerce will be holding an installment dinner on January 26, 2008 and that the State of the City address will be held on February 13, 2008. \r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r No one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the December 12, 2007 City Council meeting.\r\r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2008-241, establishing an Historic Preservation Ordinance for the City of Calabasas by amending Titles 2 and 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code to add Chapter 2.30 (establishment of an Historic Preservation Commission) and 17.36 (Historic Preservation Ordinance) and to amend Chapter 17.90 (add definitions for Historic Preservation) and Section 17.18.040 (eliminate conflicts with the Scenic Corridor Ordinance).\r\r Recommendation to approve a professional services agreement with Scott Roeb Catering & Events, Inc. for catering and event planning services for the Grand Opening Gala Event for the new Civic Center.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1108, approving the cooperative agreement with the Department of Transportation for improvements to State Route 101/Lost Hills Road Freeway Interchange.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3 and 4. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Report from the Sheriff�s Department regarding support during emergencies.\r\rLt. Pat Davoren, Lost Hills Sheriff�s Station, presented the staff report. \r\r There was no action taken.\r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2008-242, amending Chapter 3.40 of the Calabasas Municipal Code relating to the Purchasing System. \r\rDr. Gary J. Lysik, Chief Financial Officer, presented the staff report. \r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2008-242. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Discussion regarding adopting Resolution No. 2008-1109, which affirms the City�s commitment to the Pontoppidan family regarding their property.\r\rErik Pontoppidan, Calabasas, spoke regarding his family�s concern regarding eminent domain action on his property and spoke in support of the resolution.\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1109 with revisions. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Discussion regarding interim recommendations on the General Plan.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director and Tom Bartlett, City Planner, presented the staff report. \r\rMelissa Olen, Calabasas, Donna Lane, Calabasas and Erik Pontoppidan, Calabasas, expressed concern over development of the west side of the City.\r\rThe Council provided direction to staff on the interim recommendations.\r\r Discussion regarding remaining undeveloped parcels in the City.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to continue the item to a date certain. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Report from Councilmember Wolfson on the Green Build Conference and discussion regarding green building initiatives.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, and Councilmember Wolfson, presented the report.\rThe City Council concurred to form a task force to design a program for green initiatives in the City.\r\r Discussion regarding potential future annexation of the Mont Calabasas community.\r\rThe City Council directed staff to bring back the annexation request as a resolution.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of December 6, 2007 to December 17, 2007.\r\r There was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Councilmember Washburn presented an update on the Civic Center Task Force.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles stated that the Library Commission will be holding a workshop regarding fundraising activities for the new Civic Center.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested that the following items be placed on a future agenda:\r\rApproving a proposal on meeting with the Congressional delegation on postal and transportation issues;\rDiscussion regarding holding a theatre festival in the City;\rDiscussion regarding emergency communications in the City be placed on a future agenda;\rDiscussion regarding procedures for individuals to contribute funds to the City for the Civic Center and Library.\r\rADJOURN \r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:54 p.m. into closed session and adjourned without reportable action from closed session at 10:54 p.m.\r\r\r\r\r_________________________________\rRobin Parker, City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00143\u0015\r01/02/08\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000